{"kind":"request","text":"CS-1: the screen host rows for the installed Counter 0.4.0.\n\nOutcome: a member opens the Counter screen at\n`https://counter.inguz.space`, and the NF-7 browser witness has an\naddress.\n\nThe fact. Counter 0.4.0 is active in the hosted room\n`counter-witness` on dap-lending as install item 2 (act `8949e952`).\nThe room Worker and the sandbox Worker hold no screen host row for\nit. The room's screen path answers 404, and so does\n`https://counter.inguz.space/`.\n\nWork:\n1. `APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS` in `apps/room/wrangler.lending.jsonc`\n   gains one row:\n   `{\"v\":1,\"screenOrigin\":\"https://counter.inguz.space\",\n   \"roomOrigin\":\"https://dap-lending.inguz.workers.dev\",\n   \"directory\":\"sc_rgtlrioy5eckfikcapmqdteiw7y4b4lrc7k6use4rqdktn4lnabq\",\n   \"item\":2,\n   \"presentation\":\"sha256:52378055c218a42c6808af21fea097b69e42b9cc52877f3cec12ad432df8ff9e\"}`\n2. `SCREEN_HOSTS` of the sandbox Worker gains\n   `{\"host\":\u003cthe same object\u003e,\"service\":\"LENDING\"}`, in the file\n   that holds the Lending row today. The two host objects are equal.\n3. Update each test that pins these two settings. Add no new test\n   file.\n\nPosition. A side head, or a rider of the AE-1 head if its gate has\nnot started. Tell me which head carries it. The paths are the two\nsettings files and the tests that pin them.\n\nAfter the landing I deploy dap-lending first and the sandbox second,\nand I read the screen address.\n\nThis request adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no\ncapability name or form, no tool family and no record model.","body":{"conditions":"The head lands on main with the gate passed and the checker's approval. The existing sandbox and deployment-smoke owners pass with the new rows. The Lending rows stay byte-equal.","target_head":"6728059211cee75dc0f6fdd104ef52a44c5f7da0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91